# `project - rename` with spaces (D-026): DS0104 with a fix; it still parses as project-rename.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | project - rename total = amount
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..47
  PIPELINE@0..46
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    PROJECT_RENAME_OP@15..46
      IDENT@15..22 "project"
      WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
      MINUS@23..24 "-"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      IDENT@25..31 "rename"
      WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
      RENAME_ITEM@32..46
        NAME@32..37
          IDENT@32..37 "total"
        WHITESPACE@37..38 " "
        EQ@38..39 "="
        WHITESPACE@39..40 " "
        NAME_REF@40..46
          IDENT@40..46 "amount"
  WHITESPACE@46..47 "\n"

error[DS0104]: operator name `project - rename` has spaces in it
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | project - rename total = amount
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an operator name is one word
  |
  = help: write `project-rename`, with no spaces

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | project-rename total = amount
which parses without errors
